      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The observed pressure spikes in the transmission hydraulic circuit are likely caused by issues with the vehicle's pressure regulator or VPC (Variable Viscosity Pilot) system. One common problem is a faulty or malfunctioning VPC solenoid or valve, which can cause irregular pressure fluctuations during shifts. Poor hydraulic fluid level, low fluid pressure, or blockages in the transmission circuit can also lead to these issues. Overheating of the transmission system is another potential cause.",
